The toggle shortcode is similar to the code-toggle, but it&rsquo;s more generic.
Usage 1&lt;/* toggle myToggleName */&gt; 2 3 &lt;/* toggle-item myToggleItemName */&gt; 4 CONTENT HERE, MARKDOWN and SHORTCODE are support. 5 &lt;/* /toggle-item */&gt; 6 7 ... 8 9&lt;/* /toggle */&gt; The myToggleName MUST be unique per page. The myToggleItemName MUST be unique per toggle. Example &lt; toggle foobar &gt;
&lt; toggle-item Foo &gt; Foo &lt; /toggle-item &gt;
&lt; toggle-item Bar &gt; Bar &lt; /toggle-item &gt;
&lt; /toggle &gt;
&lt; toggle languages &gt; &lt; toggle-item PHP &gt; &lt; highlight php &gt; echo &ldquo;hello world&rdquo; &lt; /highlight &gt; &lt; /toggle-item &gt;
&lt; toggle-item JS &gt; &lt; highlight javascript &gt; console.log(&ldquo;hello world&rdquo;) &lt; /highlight &gt; &lt; /toggle-item &gt;
&lt; toggle-item SQL &gt; &lt; highlight sql &gt; SELECT &ldquo;hello world&rdquo; &lt; /highlight &gt; &lt; /toggle-item &gt;
&lt; /toggle &gt;

